BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2nd Annual Langworthy Winery Fallfest
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTSTAMP:20261010T155734Z
UID:ad63d41948f455356f4a96ce2520@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Spend a fall afternoon enjoying local artisan booths\, grape s
 tomping\, live music from Sarah LuAnn Thompson\, horse‑drawn carriage ri
 des\, and pet adoptions with Anchor Paws Rescue. Food and treats are avail
 able from W’s Wood Fired Pizza Oven and the Two Scoops Cafe ice cream tr
 uck\, with Langworthy wine poured throughout the day. Come hungry\, sip wi
 ne\, browse handmade goods\, enjoy the music\, take a carriage ride\, stom
 p grapes\, and soak in a beautiful New England fall afternoon.\n\nSource: 
 https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/2nd-annual-langworthy-winery-fallfe
 st/111825/
LOCATION:Langworthy Farm Winery\, 308 Shore Road\, Westerly\, RI 02891
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/2nd-annual-langworthy-winery-fa
 llfest/111825/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTSTAMP:20261010T155734Z
UID:75f1278119b584c205e5b4e9e0ff@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alasdair Fraser
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTSTAMP:20261010T155734Z
UID:de8b30364d074a668fe4f104c6d9@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Blackstone River Theatre is thrilled to present a solo concert
  with Alasdair Fraser\, “the Michael Jordan of Scottish fiddling\,” sp
 anning the full spectrum between intimate chamber music and ecstatic dance
  energy. Over several decades\, Fraser has truly set the standard for fidd
 le traditional music\, thrilling audiences internationally with virtuosic 
 playing and the joyful spontaneity and sheer physical presence of his musi
 c. In recognition of his services to traditional music he was inducted int
 o the Scottish Traditional Music Hall of Fame in 2011. Since 2003 Alasdair
  has been featured in a duo with cellist Natalie Haas\, restoring the wee 
 fiddle and big fiddle partnership that flourished in eighteenth century Sc
 otland to contemporary prominence. Fraser has a concert and recording care
 er spanning over 30 years\, with a long list of awards\, accolades\, radio
  and television credits\, and feature performances on top movie soundtrack
 s including “Last of the Mohicans\,” “Titanic\,” and more. Alasdai
 r has also guested with The Chieftains\, The Waterboys\, and Itzhak Perlma
 n and has appeared on innumerable broadcasts including A Prairie Home Comp
 anion and CBS TV’s Kennedy Center Honors.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrh
 odeisland.com/event/alasdair-fraser/111060/
LOCATION:Blackstone River Theatre\, 549 Broad Street\, Cumberland\, RI 028
 64
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/alasdair-fraser/111060/
END:VEVENT
